# Grid A — S8 Call chain (analyzer post-processing)
#
# Targets: architecture_explain + ReqCallChain + ShapeStepList.
# The buildAnalysisIR → ... → gate.Run chain is the canonical
# analyzer post-processing pipeline (CLAUDE.md §Analyzer
# post-processing: 6 numbered steps). A correct answer walks the
# steps in order; a wrong answer either skips middle nodes or
# conflates it with the runtime scheduler.
#
# Positive anchor pins the two endpoints. Negative anchor blocks the
# common failure: conflating the analyzer's static pipeline with the
# orchestrator's runTaskGraph dynamic scheduler.
ID="s8a"
NAME="call chain — analyzer post-processing buildAnalysisIR → gate.Run"
QUESTION="从 analyzer.go 的 buildAnalysisIR 到 gate.Run 之间的确定性处理链都经过哪几步？按调用顺序列出中间的关键函数。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC `buildAnalysisIR gate.Run`
# was the question's two endpoints — bar = "复述题目两端"; an answer
# "buildAnalysisIR runs analyzer logic and ends at gate.Run" PASSed
# without enumerating the chain. Verified ground truth (sequence in
# `internal/agent/analyzer.go::buildAnalysisIR` line 1280-1430):
#   1. normalizer.Normalize  → TermGraph
#   2. compiler.InferScenario → Scenario
#   3. compiler.Compile        → TaskGraph + EvidencePlan + AnswerContract
#   4. hdp.Plan                → Hypotheses (HDP)
#   5. compiler.RecomputeBudget → final budget
#   6. binder.BindByRelevance  → criterion binding
#   7. gate.RunWith / gate.Run → quality gate
# Strict-bar requires answer to surface ≥3 of the 5 numbered chain
# functions verbatim — generic "the analyzer runs several steps"
# no longer PASSes.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="buildAnalysisIR gate.Run"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(normalizer\.Normalize|TermGraph)
(compiler\.Compile|TaskGraph|EvidencePlan|RecomputeBudget)
(hdp\.Plan|hypothes|HypothesisSet|binder\.BindByRelevance)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="runTaskGraph DesignReviewer"
